# {{.ProjectName}}

A high-performance web API built with Echo framework and Go.

## Features

- 🚀 **Echo Framework**: Fast and minimalist web framework
- 📊 **Structured Logging**: Using {{.Logger}} for structured logging
{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}
- 🗄️ **Database**: {{.DatabaseDriver}} database integration
{{- if ne .DatabaseORM ""}}
- 🔧 **ORM**: {{.DatabaseORM}} for database operations
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .AuthType "jwt"}}
- 🔐 **JWT Authentication**: Secure token-based authentication
{{- else if eq .AuthType "session"}}
- 🔐 **Session Authentication**: Secure session-based authentication
{{- end}}
{{- if .EnableMetrics}}
- 📈 **Metrics**: Prometheus metrics collection
{{- end}}
{{- if .EnableTracing}}
- 🔍 **Tracing**: OpenTelemetry distributed tracing
{{- end}}
- 🐳 **Docker**: Containerized deployment
- 🧪 **Testing**: Comprehensive test suite

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Go {{.GoVersion}} or later
- Docker (optional)
{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}
{{- if eq .DatabaseDriver "postgres"}}
- PostgreSQL (or use Docker Compose)
{{- else if eq .DatabaseDriver "mysql"}}
- MySQL (or use Docker Compose)
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

### Installation

```bash
# Clone and setup
git clone <your-repo>
cd {{.ProjectName}}

# Install dependencies
make deps

# Run the application
make run
```

### Development

```bash
# Run in development mode with auto-reload
make dev

# Run tests
make test

# Run with coverage
make coverage

# Lint code
make lint
```

### Docker

```bash
# Build and run with Docker
make docker-build
make docker-run
```

{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}

### Database Setup

{{- if eq .DatabaseDriver "postgres"}}
```bash
# Using Docker Compose (recommended for development)
docker-compose up -d postgres

# Or install PostgreSQL locally and create database
createdb {{.ProjectName}}
```
{{- else if eq .DatabaseDriver "mysql"}}
```bash
# Using Docker Compose (recommended for development)
docker-compose up -d mysql

# Or install MySQL locally and create database
mysql -u root -p -e "CREATE DATABASE {{.ProjectName}};"
```
{{- else if eq .DatabaseDriver "sqlite"}}
```bash
# SQLite database will be created automatically
```
{{- end}}

```bash
# Run database migrations
make migrate-up
```
{{- end}}

## Configuration

The application can be configured using environment variables or configuration files:

- `configs/config.dev.yaml` - Development configuration
- `configs/config.prod.yaml` - Production configuration
- `configs/config.test.yaml` - Test configuration

### Environment Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `ENVIRONMENT` | Application environment | `development` |
| `{{upper .ProjectName}}_SERVER_PORT` | Server port | `8080` |
{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}
| `{{upper .ProjectName}}_DATABASE_HOST` | Database host | `localhost` |
| `{{upper .ProjectName}}_DATABASE_NAME` | Database name | `{{.ProjectName}}` |
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .AuthType "jwt"}}
| `{{upper .ProjectName}}_JWT_SECRET` | JWT secret key | **Required in production** |
{{- end}}

## API Documentation

{{- if eq .AuthType "jwt"}}
### Authentication

All protected endpoints require a valid JWT token in the Authorization header:

```
Authorization: Bearer <your-jwt-token>
```

### Auth Endpoints

- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` - User login
- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` - User registration
- `POST /api/v1/auth/logout` - User logout

{{- end}}

### Health Endpoints

- `GET /health` - Application health check
- `GET /ready` - Application readiness check

{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}

### User Endpoints

- `GET /api/v1/users` - List users
- `GET /api/v1/users/:id` - Get user by ID
- `POST /api/v1/users` - Create user
- `PUT /api/v1/users/:id` - Update user
- `DELETE /api/v1/users/:id` - Delete user

{{- end}}

{{- if .EnableMetrics}}

### Metrics

Prometheus metrics are available at `GET /metrics` (default port 9090).

{{- end}}

